This directory holds the pinned expected SHA-256 of this track's output file.

It is tracked (via this placeholder) because git cannot store an empty
directory, and the documented pinning command redirects into this path: without
the directory the redirect fails and the SHA-256 gate can never be satisfied.

On Oct 30 06:00 UTC, write ONE file here named aggregates.txt.sha256, containing the
64 hex characters of the sample's hash.

Write it as UTF-8 WITHOUT a BOM, or the first "hex" character will be the BOM
and the pin will not parse. In Windows PowerShell 5.1 the `>` operator writes
UTF-16LE, so use the explicit form in docs/CAMPAIGN-STATUS.md rather than `>`.

No placeholder hash is committed here on purpose: a file containing
"TODO-fill-this-in" used to satisfy the lockdown's is_file() check and certify
a correctness gate that could not be checked. Now an unparsable pin is a FAIL.
